{"id":"h066","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"science-physics","question":"What is the total charge in coulombs of $75.0 \\mathrm{~kg}$ of electrons?\nIs the correct answer \"$-1.32$ $10^{13} \\mathrm{C}$\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The proposed answer of -1.32 × 10^13 C is correct.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"An electron has charge -1.602 × 10^-19 C and mass 9.109 × 10^-31 kg.","confidence":0.98,"lean":1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The charge-to-mass ratio of the electron is about -1.759 × 10^11 C/kg.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Multiplying the ratio by 75.0 kg gives about -1.32 × 10^13 C.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The sign is negative because electrons are negatively charged.","confidence":0.98,"lean":1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The missing multiplication sign in the proposed answer could cause misreading.","confidence":0.5,"lean":-1,"theta":0.7854,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The only sensible reading of the proposed string is -1.32 × 10^13 C.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Rounding to three significant figures is the only source of small differences and matches the data's precision.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The notation issue is merely cosmetic and does not affect correctness.","confidence":0.92,"lean":1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.2,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":